WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.903 --> 00:00:09.736
(laughter)

00:00:09.736 --> 00:00:11.310
- [Mark] All right. What is your name?

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.143
- Royalty.

00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:13.010
- Royalty?

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:13.843
- Yes.

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:14.807
- [Mark] Royalty, where'd you grow up?

00:00:14.807 --> 00:00:16.420
Where are you from?

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.190
- [Royalty] Well, I grew up in Watts.

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:19.023
- [Mark] South Central?

00:00:19.023 --> 00:00:19.856
- [Royalty] Yes.

00:00:19.856 --> 00:00:20.700
- [Mark] And tell me about your family,

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.353
you grew up with both your parents?

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.773
- [Royalty] Yes, my step-dad and my mom.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.150
- And how was your childhood?

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.800
- Well, in the beginning it was okay.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.600
But then, we ended up in foster care.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.290
And, like, we were separated.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.360
- Who's we? You and your...

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.530
- Me and my siblings.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.363
- Oh, I see.

00:00:44.363 --> 00:00:45.390
- It was like, six of us.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.660
I basically was taking care of my sisters,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.357
because my step-dad
had a gambling problem.

00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:56.360
- Oh, okay.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.360
- And, my mom, she
basically dipped, like left,

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:05.160
like for sometimes weeks, sometimes days.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.570
And I was left taking care of my siblings.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:08.470
- Are you the oldest?

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.063
- Yeah. With a twin.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.001
- Oh, I see. Okay.

00:01:12.001 --> 00:01:12.834
- So...

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.650
I was just raised taking care of them

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:18.610
at a young age. I was like six years old,

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.590
taking care of my siblings.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.010
- And then how were your teenage years?

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:29.010
- Actually, I spent- thirteen years old

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.027
from juvenile hall. I
went from juvenile hall

00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:34.529
to the compound.

00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:37.170
Then, from the compound

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.421
I went to prison.

00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:40.650
- What were you in juvenile
hall for? And prison?

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.050
- Uh, for killing the
person that sodomized me.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:44.950
- Who'd you kill?

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:45.783
- My foster dad.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.050
- Oh, so in the foster home you got-

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.670
he was molesting you?

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.487
And how did you murder him?

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.520
- Um, I found the gun with somebody that

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.750
took me in. Basically
he knew what I wanted

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.550
to do right then and then.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.950
And, woke- went to the place and

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:08.286
woke him up. Gave him
a choice and told him

00:02:08.286 --> 00:02:12.140
if... you have a choice, like, you either

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.070
going to like do it yourself while I

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:20.870
have a gun pointing, or I'm going to do it

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.970
because either way you have to go, because

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:25.701
you shouldn't have to do that to

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.593
a twelve-year-old girl.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:30.960
You know, like...

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:33.993
- Wow.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.857
- It's- because, it really fucks with you,

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:39.860
you know?

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.693
- Absolutely.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.490
- And to do that to me
and then throw me out

00:02:45.328 --> 00:02:50.023
with nothing? Like, no
clothes, I was just trash.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.870
You know, it's devastating.

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:57.663
- Yeah. So you ended up
in prison for how long?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.610
- From thirteen, I
didn't get out until 25.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.120
I'm basically 27 now.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.927
- Oh my god, so you just got out.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.343
- And it's like, I had dreams, you know.

00:03:11.269 --> 00:03:16.100
To become a singer, write poems,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.586
and all that, and it was basically like

00:03:18.586 --> 00:03:20.223
he took that away from me.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.900
- [Mark] Yeah, you spent half your life

00:03:24.312 --> 00:03:25.212
in prison or jail.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.950
So, do you still stay in touch

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.150
with any of your family?

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.650
- [Royalty] Most of them I do.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.900
But me and my twin
basically don't get along.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.740
Because we always argue, she felt because

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.873
when I was a newborn I had health issues.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.533
I basically, when Mom gave birth to me,

00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:03.390
I basically flat-lined.
I stopped breathing,

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.668
I turned blue and purple,
I was pronounced dead

00:04:05.668 --> 00:04:10.668
for three hours. And my family basically

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.943
was treating me like royalty, you know.

00:04:16.802 --> 00:04:19.110
Whenever I needed
something they was there,

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.834
and she hated me because of that.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:22.667
- [Mark] Oh.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.532
- [Royalty] So, I don't talk to her.

00:04:24.532 --> 00:04:28.430
My step-dad, I talk to. My real dad,

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:30.030
I'm barely just getting to know.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.160
- And where are you living now?

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.090
- Right now, I'm living in a tent.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:40.923
- In Skid Row?

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.120
Are you using any drugs that are out here?

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:46.970
You're not using?

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.750
- Maybe I smoke weed. Because I'm still

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:56.750
trying to do my music, and everything.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.620
But it's hard when you have

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.870
that record on you.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:01.703
- Absolutely.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.550
- It's hard to get a job.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.044
- It's gonna follow you everywhere you go.

00:05:06.044 --> 00:05:06.877
- Yeah.

00:05:08.773 --> 00:05:10.423
- And how do you support yourself now?

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.370
- Right now, I have two bikes.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.583
One, I sell.

00:05:19.214 --> 00:05:21.157
I sold my bikes and sometimes

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.610
family or friends I sing for

00:05:27.462 --> 00:05:30.330
look out for meeting and..

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.880
- Get out, dating guys like a lot

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.740
of the girls do? You do that, too?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:37.690
Yeah. It's a common story down here.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.373
- Yeah, I used to do it.

00:05:41.142 --> 00:05:44.036
But then I felt like I was better,

00:05:44.036 --> 00:05:47.060
I felt degraded. And basically it was

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.780
giving me flashbacks. So, yeah, I stopped.

00:05:52.973 --> 00:05:54.931
- And do you have any friends?

00:05:54.931 --> 00:05:56.187
- I have very few.

00:05:56.187 --> 00:05:57.748
- You kind of had a big chunk of your life

00:05:57.748 --> 00:06:01.820
taken away from you, so it's hard to

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.037
make friends, right?

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.083
- Yeah, because it's hard to trust.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.809
- What kind of thoughts
go through your head?

00:06:14.809 --> 00:06:18.270
What do you wish was different about your

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.840
childhood that might
have- I mean, certainly

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.390
not having a step-dad molesting you would

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:24.860
be a big one.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.600
- I wish I could have
thought the situation

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:33.155
out instead of not thinking and

00:06:33.155 --> 00:06:38.155
just doing it. I could have thought

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:40.603
about the situation better.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.590
- Did you tell, was it
your mom, that could

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.520
have done something?

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.763
- My step-mom passed away-

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.622
- It was your foster mom, your foster mom

00:06:51.622 --> 00:06:53.160
could have done something, right?

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.270
- She passed away.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:55.470
- Oh, so the step-dad-

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.830
- She passed away in my lap,

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:57.730
she had a seizure.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.450
And right after she passed away,

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.923
that's when all hell broke loose.

00:07:08.705 --> 00:07:09.538
- Oh jeez.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.170
- And all the thoughts
ran through my head,

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:18.870
like, did he do it? Because he showed

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.077
no emotion. So, basically I was just

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:31.560
on my own. Like, foster homes don't care.

00:07:31.976 --> 00:07:35.003
The social workers, they
say they do, though.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.107
- You've never had anybody
that cared for you.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:45.210
- No. The only person
that cared- showed that

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.117
cared was my son.

00:07:48.117 --> 00:07:48.950
- Oh, you have a son?

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.870
- I have a four year
old. About to be five.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:51.980
In a foster home.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:52.813
- He's in a foster home.

00:07:52.813 --> 00:07:54.470
Do you ever get a chance to talk to him,

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.303
or see him?

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.532
- They took him away
because he's artistic.

00:07:59.532 --> 00:08:00.783
- Autistic?

00:08:01.672 --> 00:08:04.918
- And they say with my anger issues and

00:08:04.918 --> 00:08:09.918
me having blackouts that I'm not

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.690
able to take responsibility and take care

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.770
of my son unless I have joint custody.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:19.553
- When you have blackouts,
what causes blackouts?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.543
- My anger. I guess
from when I flat-lined,

00:08:28.029 --> 00:08:31.790
I just have blackouts to
where I can't remember

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:32.990
and then I have seizures

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.763
because I had brain trauma.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.173
- From your birth?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.370
- Yes.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.830
- Are you on medication for that?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.343
- I had supposed to take it, but I don't.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.010
I mainly smoke weed

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.913
to basically calm it.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:00.433
That's it.

00:09:04.765 --> 00:09:06.740
- Do you have any plans for your future?

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.383
Anything you'd like to see happen?

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:16.363
- Basically follow my career, my dream.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.610
I already started writing poems

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:25.610
and putting them on Hello Poetry,

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.530
and I'm already doing music,

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:33.893
recording myself, and I love that.

00:09:36.348 --> 00:09:39.670
- Is writing music and poetry, you find it

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.400
helpful, therapeutic for-

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.233
- Yeah

00:09:42.233 --> 00:09:43.066
- What you're going through?

00:09:43.066 --> 00:09:43.899
- Yeah

00:09:43.899 --> 00:09:44.732
- Yeah, I'll bet it is.

00:09:44.732 --> 00:09:46.720
- [Royalty] It actually keep me calm.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:48.620
Especially music, like when I get

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:49.620
nervous or something

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.033
I start singing.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.630
- Yeah, you're a beautiful singer.

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.942
I heard you sing just now.

00:09:56.942 --> 00:09:57.775
(laugther)

00:09:57.775 --> 00:09:58.608
While I was setting up.

00:09:58.608 --> 00:09:59.608
- Thank you.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.770
- All right Royalty,
well thank you so much

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.574
for talking to me and sharing your story.

00:10:04.574 --> 00:10:05.407
- Thank you.

00:10:05.407 --> 00:10:07.500
- And good luck with your life now that

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.533
you're finally free.

00:10:08.533 --> 00:10:09.450
(laughter)

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.283
- Yes.

